#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example 3: Graph 3-coloring (Max-3-Cut) {#example-3-graph-3-coloring-max-3-cut}"
msgstr "Ejemplo 3: Coloreado de grafos con 3 colores (Max-3-Cut) {#example-3-graph-3-coloring-max-3-cut}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Max-$k$-Cut problem partitions the vertices of a graph into $k$ groups to maximize the number of edges whose endpoints belong to different groups. For $k = 3$ this is equivalent to finding a 3-coloring that maximizes cross-color edges.\n"
msgstr "El problema Max-$k$-Cut divide los vértices de un grafo en $k$ grupos para maximizar el número de aristas cuyos extremos pertenecen a grupos diferentes. Para $k = 3$, esto equivale a encontrar un coloreado de 3 colores que maximice las aristas entre colores distintos.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Formally, assign each node $i \\in V$ to one of $k$ groups with binary variables $x_{i,c}$ for color $c \\in \\{1, \\ldots, k\\}$. The one-hot constraint $\\sum_c x_{i,c} = 1$ for each node enforces a unique assignment. The objective maximizes cross-group edges:\n"
msgstr "Formalmente, se asigna cada nodo $i \\in V$ a uno de los $k$ grupos mediante variables binarias $x_{i,c}$ para el color $c \\in \\{1, \\ldots, k\\}$. La restricción one-hot $\\sum_c x_{i,c} = 1$ para cada nodo garantiza una asignación única. El objetivo maximiza las aristas entre grupos:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\min \\sum_{(u,v) \\in E} \\sum_c x_{u,c} \\, x_{v,c}\\\\\n"
"\\text{s.t.} \\sum_{c} x_{i,c} = 1 \\quad \\forall i \\in  V\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\min \\sum_{(u,v) \\in E} \\sum_c x_{u,c} \\, x_{v,c}\\\\\n"
"\\text{s.t.} \\sum_{c} x_{i,c} = 1 \\quad \\forall i \\in  V\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The one-hot constraints are ideal for XY-mixers, which the optimizer handles natively.\n"
msgstr "Las restricciones one-hot son ideales para los mezcladores XY, que el optimizador maneja de forma nativa.\n"

